Let me look at the diff more carefully. The change is clear from the PR diff:

**Removed code (lines 4421-4428 in the original):**
```c
    /* x86 has an upper limit of 15 bytes for an instruction. Since we
     * do not want to decode and generate IR for an illegal
     * instruction, the following check limits the instruction size to
     * 25 bytes: 14 prefix + 1 opc + 6 (modrm+sib+ofs) + 4 imm */
    if (s->pc - pc_start > 14) {
        goto illegal_op;
    }
```

This check was in the `next_byte` prefix-collection loop of `disas_insn()`. It was an early bail-out that jumped to `illegal_op` if more than 14 prefix bytes were consumed.

